{title: 210 - Wake, Awake for the Night Is Flying}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Jesus Christ}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[C]Wake, awake, for [F#dim]night is flying,
[G#m]The watchmen on [Am]the heights are crying,
[Am]Awake, Jerusalem, [Em]arise!
[G7]Midnight's solemn [Am]hour is tolling,
[C]His chariot wheels are nearer rolling,
[C]He comes; [F]prepare, ye [Am]virgins wise.
[Dm]Rise up with willing feet
[G7]Go forth, the Bridegroom [C]meet; Alleluia!
[C]Bear through the night your well-trimmed light,
[C]Speed forth to join the marriage rite.

Verse 2:
[C]Zion hears the watchmen [F#dim]singing,
[G#m]Her heart with deep delight [Am]is springing,
[Am]She wakes, she rises [Em]from her gloom;
[G7]Forth her Bridegroom [Am]comes, all-glorious,
[C]In grace arrayed, by truth victorious;
[C]Her Star is [F]risen, her [Am]Light is come!
[Dm]All hail, incarnate Lord,
[G7]Our crown, and our reward! [C]Alleluia!
[C]We haste along, in pomp and song,
[C]And gladsome join the marriage throng.

Verse 3:
[C]Lamb of God, the heavens [F#dim]adore Thee,
[G#m]And men and angels [Am]sing before Thee,
[Am]With harp and cymbal's clearest [Em]tone.
[G7]By the pearly gates [Am]in wonder
[C]We stand, and swell the voice of thunder,
[C]That echoes round Thy dazzling throne.
[C]No vision [F]ever [Am]brought,
[Dm]No ear hath ever caught,
[G7]Such bliss [C]and joy;
[C]We raise the song, we swell the throng,
[C]To praise Thee ages all along.
